            <ArticleTitle>[Right-sided lower abdominal pain and diarrhea of a young diabetic woman].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>733-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1024/1661-8157/a000161</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 24-years old diabetic women hospitalised because of right-sided lower abdominal pain and diarrhea. She fulminantly developed shock before appendectomy could be performed and was transferred to intensive care unit. Hypotension remained and laparoscopy revealed primary peritonitis and toxic shock syndrome by Group A Streptococcus which was cultivated in blood and ascites. Therapy with penicilline and clindamycine resolved symptoms. During hospitalisation Clostridium difficile colitis occurred. This complication leaded to prolonged hospitalisation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
